Q: How can I move a &lt;div&gt; continuously at every given time-interval? A: <p>Avoid using <code>margin</code> to <em>move</em> stuff around, since it will cause layout thrashing / reflow, and margin has no support for GPU acceleration.<br />
Use <code>translate</code> instead:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const myDiv = document.querySelector("#a");
let x = 0;

const moveDiv = () =&gt; myDiv.style.setProperty("--x", x += 10);
const moveItv = setInterval(moveDiv, 1000);
// clearInterval(moveItv); // When needed</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>#a {
  display: inline-flex;
  transition: translate 0.8s;
  translate: calc(var(--x, 0) * 1px) 0;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div id="a"&gt;BELLA&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: My SELECT query is removing NULL value row A: <p>Put the filters into the <code>JOIN</code> condition:</p>
<pre class="lang-sql prettyprint-override"><code>select c.custid AS &quot;Customer  ID&quot;
,      c.name   AS &quot;Customer Name&quot;
,      s.ename  AS &quot;Sales Rep&quot;
from   customer c
       left outer join emp s
       on (   c.repid = s.empno
          AND s.ename not like '%R'
          AND s.ename not like '%R_')
order by c.name;
</code></pre>
<p>If you have the filters in the <code>WHERE</code> clause then <code>s.ename</code> must be non-<code>NULL</code> and it effectively converts the <code>LEFT OUTER JOIN</code> to an <code>INNER JOIN</code>.</p>
<hr />
<p>Alternatively, you could use the filters in the <code>WHERE</code> clause and add another filter to check for <code>NULL</code> values:</p>
<pre class="lang-sql prettyprint-override"><code>select c.custid AS &quot;Customer  ID&quot;
,      c.name   AS &quot;Customer Name&quot;
,      s.ename  AS &quot;Sales Rep&quot;
from   customer c
       left outer join emp s
       on (c.repid = s.empno)
WHERE (   s.ename not like '%R'
      AND s.ename not like '%R_')
OR    s.empno IS NULL             -- Check for outer joined rows
order by c.name;
</code></pre>
<p>But it usually more comprehensible to put those filters into the join condition.</p>

Q: Is it possible to use ControlValueAccessor to bind a FormArray to a custom component in Angular? A: <p>No it is not, since <code>formControl</code> and <code>formControlName</code> both expect a <code>FormControl</code>, which <code>FormArray</code> does not extend.</p>
<p>You don't need <code>ControlValueAccessor</code>. Simply pass the <code>FormArray</code> as an input. If you want it optional make it a union type:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>public readonly items = input.required&lt;
  DummyItem[] | FormArray&lt;DummyItemForm&gt;
&gt;();

protected readonly itemFormArray = computed(() =&gt; {
  const items = this.items();
  if (!Array.isArray(items)) return items;
  return this.fb.array(items.map((i) =&gt; App.buildItemFormGroup(this.fb, i)));
});
</code></pre>
<p>and in the template iterate over the controls:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>@for (item of itemFormArray().controls; track $index) {
  Dummy Item ({{item.controls.id.value}}):
  &lt;input [formControl]=&quot;item.controls.field1&quot;/&gt;&lt;br&gt;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Here is a <a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/stackblitz-starters-eoxuchd8?file=src%2Fmain.ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer">full example</a>.</p>
